# Initial Setup's Battery Monitor 2 page, ported from
# GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigBatteryMonitoring2.cs.
#
# The claim: Activate binds the monitor and pin combos, fills the capacity and calibration boxes
# from the second battery's parameters and readings (ConfigBatteryMonitoring2.cs:17-62); the
# capacity box, left, asks the vehicle's table and says the feature is not enabled when
# BATT2_CAPACITY is missing (:70-89); the measured voltage, on Enter, needs a divider to scale
# (:91-119, 206-210); the monitor combo writes BATT2_MONITOR itself. The write is proved by the
# vehicle's echo, and put back.
#
# SITL's copter lists BATT2_MONITOR 0 and, with the second monitor off, none of its other
# parameters: the pin combos stay disabled, the capacity keeps the Designer's 2200, and the
# divider and amps-per-volt boxes are empty. The calibration arithmetic and the other boxes'
# writes need a second battery SITL does not have; the unit tests in
# crates/mp-gui/src/config/battery_monitor2.rs cover them.
#
# A config.xml of its own, so the machine's Mission Planner's low-battery alert does not tick the
# box.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-battery2.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
#
# A run that stops half way can leave BATT2_MONITOR at 3; the first expectation on it then fails
# until a fresh SITL.

env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
screen params
window 1600x1200
settle 6

click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.BATT2_MONITOR 0

click tab-setup
expect config.battery2.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigBatteryMonitoring2
settle 2
expect setup.page ConfigBatteryMonitoring2
expect config.battery2.active true
expect config.battery2.enabled true

# What Activate read.
expect config.battery2.monitor 0
expect config.battery2.monitor.text Disabled
expect config.battery2.monitor.enabled true
expect config.battery2.voltpin.enabled false
expect config.battery2.currpin.enabled false
expect config.battery2.capacity 2200
expect config.battery2.measured 0
expect config.battery2.voltage 0
expect config.battery2.speech false
expect config.battery2.readouts >= 1
expect config.battery2.write none

# The capacity, typed and left for the monitor combo: BATT2_CAPACITY is not listed.
click battery2-capacity
expect config.battery2.editing battery2-capacity
key ctrl+u
type 3000
click battery2-BATT2_MONITOR
settle 1
expect config.battery2.capacity 3000
expect config.battery2.message This feature is not enabled in your firmware.
expect config.battery2.write none
click battery2-message-ok
expect config.battery2.message none

# The monitor's list is down: Analog Voltage Only, then Disabled again.
click battery2-BATT2_MONITOR-3
settle 2
expect config.battery2.monitor 3
expect config.battery2.monitor.text Analog Voltage Only
expect config.battery2.write BATT2_MONITOR 3 accepted
expect params.value.BATT2_MONITOR 3
click battery2-BATT2_MONITOR
click battery2-BATT2_MONITOR-0
settle 2
expect config.battery2.write BATT2_MONITOR 0 accepted
expect params.value.BATT2_MONITOR 0
expect config.battery2.message none

# The measured voltage on Enter: no divider to scale.
click battery2-measured
key Return
settle 1
expect config.battery2.message ~ Invalid number entered
click battery2-message-ok
expect config.battery2.writes.pending 0

# Deactivate sets _startup: the box left as the page goes writes nothing.
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
settle 1
expect config.battery2.active false
expect config.battery2.message none
expect params.value.BATT2_MONITOR 0
